4. Mapbox Rate-Limit & 429 Console Shield Architecture
To prevent Mapbox rate-limiting (HTTP 429) from polluting the browser console or breaking tile loading during rapid camera flights, NEXUS implements a zero-rate-limit architectural shield:

Pre-Request Rerouting via transformRequest: Before any raster satellite tile request is dispatched to api.mapbox.com/v4/mapbox.satellite, Mapbox's transformRequest intercepts the URL and rewrites it to: $$\text{https://server.arcgisonline.com/ArcGIS/rest/services/World\_Imagery/MapServer/tile/}\{z\}/\{y\}/\{x\}$$
Zero Quota Limits: ESRI World Imagery provides unlimited global bandwidth and sub-meter satellite resolution.
Result: Zero requests hit Mapbox raster tile servers; zero 429 errors occur.
AWS Open Data Terrarium for 3D Mountain Elevation: Instead of querying proprietary DEM elevation tiles, mountain terrain (Entoto Ridge and the Ethiopian Highlands) is dynamically powered by AWS S3 Open Data Terrarium: $$\text{https://s3.amazonaws.com/elevation-tiles-prod/terrarium/}\{z\}/\{x\}/\{y\}\text{.png}$$
